RISC3D test kit 29 (prototype, 14 November 2026)
================================================

Kit 28's results: with lighting off, TORCS's textures draw right on the
GPU; with it on, they don't. Fog and colour material aren't the cause.

This kit narrows it down two ways:

 - Lit (double-click) draws TORCS's lighting, with its light and
   materials, on a textured plane, in six parts (top row: unlit, car
   material, TORCS's other material; bottom row: no specular, no colour
   material, normal not in an array). The litlinux script draws the same with
   Linux's Mesa directly. If Linux's picture is wrong too, it's a bug in
   the Pi's Mesa, not RISC3D's.
 - replay redraws your TORCS recording with the specular highlights off
   (NoSpec), then with the emission off (NoEmis).

Steps
-----
 1. Unzip RISC3DTest into HardDisc4, replacing kit 28.
 2. In RiSH's Root shell:
      apt-get install /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/riscos-risc3d_0.17-1_arm64.deb
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/litlinux
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/replay /riscos/3d/recorded/ctx-477.r3d 240
 3. Double-click Lit.

